      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents#1",
      "content_hash": "sha256:adf95589fe3f09e3ca842a863f5464aae3f358d6fbde0e5951dfe2ea7f68c7bf",
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
        "Part 5 Data Capture and Indexing",
        "Word Constituents"
      ],
      "internal_refs": [
        "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents"
      ],
      "kind": "body",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "page_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents",
      "provisions": [],
      "tables": [],
      "text": "Note: The trade marks contained within this document are for educational purposes only. Unauthorised use of a similar or identical trade mark to the trade mark(s) of another party could result in legal action. In this topic The Breakdown of Words 'Stop' Words Letters Letters or Words Monograms Letters Which Occur Within a Word or Attached to Words Letters That Stand Out as a Separate Feature in a Word Typescript or Punctuation Symbols Accents, umlauts, diacritics Numbers OZZ, EASY and QUICK phonetics Domain Names"
    },
    {
      "cases": [],
      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/the-breakdown-of-words",
      "content_hash": "sha256:6eda374ce39d3514fafc4dfecb597cc8c2c39e9e54c3dc8e3b786ad96e045353",
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
        "Part 5 Data Capture and Indexing",
        "Word Constituents",
        "The Breakdown of Words"
      ],
      "internal_refs": [],
      "kind": "body",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "page_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents",
      "provisions": [],
      "tables": [],
      "text": "If the mark is represented in such a way that it appears as separate elements, then it will be separated out and the individual components indexed. Transcript symbols, different styles of font, different size of lettering and different colouring or shading are examples of ways that words can be divided into separate elements. For instance the elements in the word below are entered as separate constituents: The constituents are: SAGINOMIYA, SAGI, NO, MIYA Similarly the word mark CoGel would include constituents CO and GEL. If however, the trade mark appears as a single word (all in one font) it is indexed as a single word. Should the single word contain stand-out letters or numbers, the letters and numbers are indexed separately so that someone searching for the particular letters or numbers can pick up the mark. Separating all marks into individual elements when they are not represented as separate words would clutter the full word search facility and make it ineffective."
    },
    {
      "cases": [],
      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/stop-words",
      "content_hash": "sha256:73157f7f48f7a430aeba244a93d6fd85f81fd5d1b4e889e7e268774581f240de",
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
        "Part 5 Data Capture and Indexing",
        "Word Constituents",
        "'Stop' Words"
      ],
      "internal_refs": [],
      "kind": "body",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "page_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents",
      "provisions": [],
      "tables": [],
      "text": "'Stop' words (noise words) are words which are usually insignificant and not used in searching, for example, A, TO, IS, OF and AND. These words are not automatically generated as constituents. However, they are added when they are emphasised or in italics as in 'THE Hotel' or 'THE VALET', or 'WORLD OF …', 'IMAGES OF NATURE', 'FREEDOM OF SPEECH'."
    },
    {
      "cases": [],
      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/letters",
      "content_hash": "sha256:5df86a35ce1898999fed56935486fb54827ce055c3d273def6e7c52513934940",
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
        "Part 5 Data Capture and Indexing",
        "Word Constituents",
        "Letters"
      ],
      "internal_refs": [],
      "kind": "body",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "page_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents",
      "provisions": [],
      "tables": [],
      "text": "Letters occur in trade marks as single letters, a group of letters not forming a word, or a word rendered as letters. In addition, when a group of letters is clearly an acronym, although it spells a word, it is indexed as letters. To indicate a letter or letters the constituent LTR is used. Where there is a single letter in the trade mark, # is added to the constituents as well as LTR. A constituent with an equals sign prefix is added to the constituent for groups of letters. It is useful in enabling searchers to distinguish between a group of letters and the same letters used as a word."
    },
    {
      "cases": [],
      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/letters-or-words",
      "content_hash": "sha256:556e422eaa37afce102826b98575dc32b1d0ea52c1e9d488ed7493e75420fd9b",
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
        "Part 5 Data Capture and Indexing",
        "Word Constituents",
        "Letters or Words"
      ],
      "internal_refs": [],
      "kind": "body",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "page_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents",
      "provisions": [],
      "tables": [],
      "text": "Some two-letter words such as IS, ON, AS, LA etc can also be letters. It is usually easy to differentiate the two because of the context in which they appear. If the elements are represented as letters they are indexed as letter marks with both the preceding = sign and LTR. Two-letter words in marks are simply indexed as they appear. Similarly, common abbreviations such as Mr, Dr, St or Mt would be treated as words unless they are represented in an unusual fashion and may be regarded as letters. The full words MISTER, DOCTOR, STREET, MOUNT would also be added."
    },
    {
      "cases": [],
      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/monograms",
      "content_hash": "sha256:ed7b78f92f39be063b9a71afeb1b9cb2d852162f01be8b5cd564ca798de9b564",
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
        "Part 5 Data Capture and Indexing",
        "Word Constituents",
        "Monograms"
      ],
      "internal_refs": [],
      "kind": "body",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "page_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents",
      "provisions": [],
      "tables": [],
      "text": "Monograms are groups of letters for which the sequence is unclear. These letters are firstly indexed in the intended sequence of letters, if known. Then, the letters are entered in alphabetical order. The word phrase should specify the most likely order of letters. For example the constituents for the mark below would be YSL, LSY, =YSL, =LSY LTR."
    },
    {
      "cases": [],
      "chunk_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents/letters-which-occur-within-a-word-or-attached-to-words",
      "content_hash": "sha256:b7338893bd386dfd40cbd91bb7976082ed0abf670c9c3fbc82ac99094268e307",
      "fragment": null,
      "heading_path": [
        "Part 5 Data Capture and Indexing",
        "Word Constituents",
        "Letters Which Occur Within a Word or Attached to Words"
      ],
      "internal_refs": [],
      "kind": "body",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "page_ref": "TMM/Part5/x-word-constituents",
      "provisions": [],
      "tables": [
        {
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "text": "Trade Mark"
              },
